1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,670
Flamingos aren't born pink.

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:03,850
Their chicks hatch fluffy and grey.

3
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:10,170
The pink comes from their food: tiny shrimp and algae full of orange-red pigments called carotenoids,

4
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:12,290
the same kind that make carrots orange.

5
00:00:12,790 --> 00:00:17,130
A flamingo's body pulls out those pigments and packs them into its growing feathers,

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,450
legs and beak.

7
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,330
Take them away, and new feathers grow in pale.

8
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:24,450
That's why zoos add pigment to their food.

9
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:27,770
And in mating season, flamingos even wear makeup,

10
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:31,870
rubbing pink oil from a gland near their tail all over their feathers.

11
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,260
So that pink isn't really theirs at all,

12
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:34,667
because
